From: Project Luma
Subject: [PATCH] display: start unconfigured desktop monitors at 100 percent

Keep explicit global scale overrides and stored monitor arrangements. Only
the automatic desktop fallback starts at 1.0; handheld profiles continue to
choose scale from their panel DPI. No profile or monitors.xml is rewritten.

--- a/src/backends/meta-monitor.c
+++ b/src/backends/meta-monitor.c
@@ -2420,6 +2420,13 @@
                                                &global_scaling_factor))
     return global_scaling_factor;
 
+  /* This fallback is used when no saved monitor configuration supplies a
+   * scale. Desktop installs start at 100%; a later explicit display choice
+   * stays in monitors.xml. Handheld profiles retain their DPI-based default.
+   */
+  if (g_strcmp0 (g_getenv ("LUMA_DEVICE_CLASS"), "handheld") != 0)
+    return 1.0f;
+
   return calculate_scale (monitor, monitor_mode, constraints);
 }
 
